Associations: When a function is associated with any components such as button, workflow, kiosk ,blueprint, schedules then it will be shown under Associations  References: When a existing standalone function is being called by another function named A , then that A function will be shown under Refeences 

When the existing standalone function is called by client using var response = ZDK.Apps.CRM.Functions.execute("Standalonewebhook"); then it is not listed I the references   Dependences: When a function that can be automation or anytype calls a other standalone function named B, then that B function will be listed under Dependences

1. Associations (CRM Features) When a standalone function is linked directly to a CRM component—such as a Custom Button, Workflow, Blueprint, Schedule, or Kiosk—that component will be shown under the Associations tab.
2. References (Inbound Deluge Calls) When your existing standalone function is called by another Deluge function (Function A) using standard syntax, Function A will be shown under the References tab. This tells you "who is calling me."
3. Dependencies (Outbound Deluge Calls) When your function (whether automation or standalone) calls another standalone function (Function B), Function B will be listed under the Dependencies tab. This tells you "who I am calling."
4. Exclusions (What the References Tab MISSES) The References static scanner has strict blind spots. Callers will NOT be listed in the References tab in these scenarios:
* Client Scripts: When the standalone function is called by a client using JavaScript, such as: var response = ZDK.Apps.CRM.Functions.execute("Standalonewebhook");
* External API Calls: When the function is triggered by an outside source (like a third-party app, a website, or Postman) using the REST API or an API Key.

Exhaustive References Coverage

The References tab strictly tracks native Deluge function-to-function calls. Other CRM features are tracked separately under the Associations tab. Based on this distinction, the classification is as follows:
* INCLUDED: Function-to-function calls written in Deluge and helper functions written in Deluge are included in the References tab and will appear there.
* EXCLUDED: Workflows, Blueprints, Schedules, Custom Buttons, and disabled CRM components are excluded from the References tab. However, these components are tracked separately under the Associations tab.
* EXCLUDED: Widgets, Client Scripts, SlyteUI, externally hosted code, ZDK calls such as ZDK.Apps.CRM.Functions.execute, and ZOHO.CRM.FUNCTIONS.execute or equivalent calls are excluded from the References tab.
Therefore, an empty References tab only indicates that no native Deluge function-to-function references are identified there; it should not be interpreted as proof that no other CRM component or external mechanism can invoke the function.

